            "Most invoice intake problems in accounts payable outsourcing start before the work is done: the request is accepted without a source, a deadline, or a clear boundary around what the operator may change. The cost shows up later as a reopened case, an unexplained duplicate invoice rate change, or a correction that takes longer than the original task. Make the queue owner visible for every invoice intake item, and give that owner the authority to pause the work when the evidence is not enough. A queue that mixes new requests with corrections will overstate demand and understate the time spent repairing earlier work. For the October 28 review at Outsource Accounts Payable, log the invoice intake check with the invoice image and the duplicate invoice rate result.",
