            "A accounts payable outsourcing team can look responsive while the vendor master record trail is too thin to support a correction, a customer answer, or a review by controller. When the record cannot show what changed, AP and finance managers cannot separate a process problem from a person problem, so coaching becomes guesswork. Use the approval workflow as the destination of record, and use the invoice image to prove what the operator saw before making the change. If controller cannot name the desired outcome, the request is not ready for the vendor master record queue. The controller decision on vendor master record should be dated October 28 and linked to the invoice image.",
