            "Do not treat a forwarded email as the record itself when the governing value lives in the payment bank portal; the email may explain intent, but it does not replace the field. Attach the vendor master record to the case, label its version or date, and record the field in the payment bank portal that it supports. If the payment bank portal and the vendor master record disagree, stop the dependent action and record both values with the time each was observed. A source that cannot be opened by the reviewer is not a usable source, even if the operator can see it on their screen. The payment run review at Outsource Accounts Payable should state whether the vendor master record was current on October 28.",
            "The payment run evidence set should include the request, the approval matrix, the owner decision, the action taken, and the final value in the 1099 tracker. The reviewer should be able to open the approval matrix from the case without searching a personal drive or asking for a screenshot. Keep an exception note that explains which value was used, which was rejected, and why; a later reviewer should not have to infer the choice from the final number. The team should test one payment run case each week by reconstructing it from the evidence map alone. On October 28, Outsource Accounts Payable should compare the payment run queue count with the duplicate invoice rate denominator.",
            "If treasury lead supplies the instruction, keep the instruction and the underlying payment run together rather than replacing one with a summary of the other. Keep the original payment run and the corrected version side by side, with the reason for the change and the person who approved it. After the conflict is resolved, add a short correction entry to the payment run log and link it to both source versions. Keep the payment run in the approved repository and link it to the payment run case instead of attaching it to a personal message. The October 28 payment run note should distinguish a missing payment run from a confirmed negative."
