            "A sent message, a closed ticket, or a verbal yes is not proof that the expense policy outcome reached the record. Use a second reviewer for high-risk expense policy closures, and record the review even when the result is accepted. Do not overwrite the first close note; add a correction entry so the history remains readable. Use a consistent close reason so the monthly review can separate completed work from cancelled or duplicate requests. The October 28 evidence trail for expense policy should show the source version and the AP manager decision.",
            "The close note should be short: what changed, where it changed, who approved it, and how it was confirmed. Sample the closed expense policy cases for missing evidence, not only for speed; a fast close with no invoice image is not a strong control. If the correction affects duplicate payment, notify controller before the next dependent action. If the destination is a downstream team, keep the expense policy open until that team acknowledges receipt. For this October 28 pass, Outsource Accounts Payable should record which expense policy exception was paused and who released it."
